m2l-str;

# P1 fixture (docs/prd/ltlf-to-nfa.md, "Implementation phases" Phase 1):
# a hand-written M2L-Str source, NOT derived from any Goal formula phi (the
# mirror -> M2L-Str encoder is Phase 2).  Free second-order variables "a" and
# "b" stand in for two Goal APs; the formula "a sub b" (every position in a
# is also in b) just needs to exercise the MONA -w output shapes P1's parser
# must handle: a multi-state DFA, a mix of 0/1/don't-care ("X") transition
# guard bits, and a non-initial, non-total-alphabet accepting set.
#
# Expected `mona -q -w -n` output (verified by running mona on this file):
#
#   DFA for formula with free variables: a b
#   Initial state: 0
#   Accepting states: 1
#   Rejecting states: 2
#   Don't-care states: 0
#
#   Automaton has 3 states and 4 BDD-nodes
#   Transitions:
#   State 0: XX -> state 1
#   State 1: 0X -> state 1
#   State 1: 10 -> state 2
#   State 1: 11 -> state 1
#   State 2: XX -> state 2
#
# i.e. D has states {0,1,2}, initial state 0, accepting F_D={1}; state 2 is
# a rejecting sink.  This is deterministic + complete: state 1's guards
# {!a, a&!b, a&b} partition the full 2-bit letter space.
var2 a, b;
a sub b;
